  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 150eb (Premium) <strong>♦</strong> <strong>Fits:</strong> All Bulletproof Shields</p>\n<p><em>Many ballistic shields can provide greater levels of protection than standard riot shields, if provided the right plating and materials.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Shield Attachment.</strong> Installing this requires a DV17 Basic Tech Skill Check, and cannot be removed once installed. The shield’s HP is increased by 3. However, the shield is now considered Expensive for the purposes of repairs, maintenance, and Upgrade Expertise. Only one Superdense Layer can be installed.</p>\n<p><strong>Type:</strong> Shield Attachment<br>\n<strong>Attachment slots:</strong> 0</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Shield Attachments and Enhancements follow the Armor Attachment and Enhancement rules, but for Bulletproof Shields, including cyberware ones; not for vehicle Bulletproof Glass. Corgo's optional rule: a Bulletproof Shield with HP left puts its wielder in Cover and counts as a 2x2m/yds piece of Cover against Suppressive Fire, which they may share with one adjacent character.</li>\n<li>+3 shield HP (automated), but the shield counts as Expensive for repairs, maintenance, and Upgrade Expertise.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Armor &amp; Fashion &gt; Shields).</em></p>"
